{
  "version": 4,
  "terraform_version": "1.8.2",
  "serial": 61,
  "lineage": "08db4d26-4a45-f0a3-0869-f2da17a4bce9",
  "outputs": {
    "demo_instructions": {
      "value": "  \r\n========================================\r\nRoute 53 Failover Demo - Next Steps\r\n========================================\r\n  \r\n1. Test the instances directly:\r\n   PRIMARY:   http://34.203.35.69\r\n   SECONDARY: http://34.221.218.216\r\n     \r\n2. Test health check endpoints:\r\n   PRIMARY:   http://34.203.35.69/health\r\n   SECONDARY: http://34.221.218.216/health\r\n  \r\n3. Create Route 53 Hosted Zone and Failover Records:\r\n   - Create a hosted zone for your domain\r\n   - Create PRIMARY A record:\r\n     * Name: failover.yourdomain.com\r\n     * Type: A\r\n     * Value: 34.203.35.69\r\n     * Routing Policy: Failover\r\n     * Failover Record Type: Primary\r\n     * Health Check: a6bac750-9a2c-4613-ba14-83ac87fe0ed9\r\n     * Record ID: primary-server\r\n     \r\n   - Create SECONDARY A record:\r\n     * Name: failover.yourdomain.com (SAME name)\r\n     * Type: A\r\n     * Value: 34.221.218.216\r\n     * Routing Policy: Failover\r\n     * Failover Record Type: Secondary\r\n     * Health Check: 1fda5dad-7a80-45e7-a093-b379ae7d0b1b\r\n     * Record ID: secondary-server\r\n  \r\n4. Test Failover:\r\n   - Browse to http://failover.yourdomain.com (should show PRIMARY - green)\r\n   - Stop primary instance: aws ec2 stop-instances --instance-ids i-00de9a72f86d53e30\r\n   - Wait 2-3 minutes for health check to fail\r\n   - Refresh browser (should show SECONDARY - red/orange)\r\n   - Start primary instance: aws ec2 start-instances --instance-ids i-00de9a72f86d53e30\r\n   - Wait for health check to recover\r\n   - Should automatically failback to PRIMARY\r\n  \r\n========================================\r\n",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "primary_eip_allocation_id": {
      "value": "eipalloc-0f6f7f70fce3bca9f",
      "type": "string"
    },
